THOUGHT: The varargs constructor directly passes the possibly-null `keyFrames` parameter to `setKeyFrames`, which assigns the field and uses `keyFrames.length`. NullAway flags that the field may not be initialized on all paths (e.g., if the argument is null, leading to NPE before assignment). To satisfy NullAway and keep behavior safe, I’ll add a null check in the constructor to replace a null varargs array with an empty array of `Object` (cast to `T[]`), ensuring `this.keyFrames` is always non-null and `setKeyFrames` is always called with a non-null array. Then I’ll run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '97,100c\  public Animation(float frameDuration, T... keyFrames) {
    this.frameDuration = frameDuration;
    if (keyFrames == null) {
      keyFrames = (T[]) new Object[0];
    }
    setKeyFrames(keyFrames);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/Animation.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "Animation.java" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

